# What a turret costs, on the real keys (owner 2026-09-17, docs/DESIGN.md
# §Settlements): the thing it shoots comes for IT. A yard with a gun in it, a
# party sent for the mast, a bolt into one of them, and that one walking back out
# of the yard to cut the gun down instead of finishing its errand.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/turret-raid.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --holding=hut,radio_mast,wind_spinner,battery_stack,battery_stack,turret \
#     --attention=0.72
#
# --holding stands the yard already built with its cells full, and --attention
# stages it at the raid line. Neither is a shortcut past the rule: nothing is
# ever sent for a place nothing has read, and it is the clerk in frame 02 that
# reads this one.
zoom 11
coast calm
wait 0.8
shot 01-a-yard-with-a-gun-in-it with holding, piece:turret, turret_armed
# Something reads the place, and what it walks off with is what brings the party.
spawn clerk
await noticed 14
wait 0.3
shot 02-a-clerk-reads-the-yard with mob:clerk, holding
await warned 25
# The window runs out and they come out of the land for the mast. The gun takes
# the nearest of them as it closes.
hour 12.6
wait 1.6
await raid 40
await party 40
await turret_hit 90
wait 0.4
shot 03-the-gun-takes-one-of-them with mob, holding
# And it turns. A raider hurt by the yard has something to deal with that is not
# the mast and is not the player: it walks at what shot it. The player's own
# swing would take it straight back, and nothing in the raids package says so —
# the fight writes where the last blow came from, and the last blow decides.
await raider_turned 60
wait 2.2
shot 04-it-turns-on-what-shot-it with mob, piece:turret
